# TryHackMe - Systems as Attack Vectors

## Overview
This room covers system attacks and potential vulnerabilities. It mentions human-led attacks such as rubber duckies, misconfigurations and software vulnerabilities. 
The room also introduces the concept of CVE numbers and asks you to look up the number of a known vulnerability.  

## Topics Covered
- Human-led attacks
- Software vulnerabilities
- Misconfigurations and potential solutions
- Supply chain vulnerabilities 

## Key Takeaways
- A SOC analyst always has to be informed about the latest exploits
- Even software-based attacks are based on human negligence in the end 
- There is a database of known exploits 

## Reflection
I believe that purely technical attacks will be carried out almost exclusively by AI in the future.

